gaps.failure_scenario:
The model writes `while True:
    try:
        time.sleep(0.05)
    except BaseException:
        pass` (a retry wrapper that catches everything is a common model pattern), or calls `input()`, `sys.stdin.read()`, `socket.recv()` or `threading.Event().wait()`. The injection is swallowed or never lands; `done` is never set; `run_script` never returns; the turn holds `turn_lock` (agents/state_machine.py:374, 960-967, TURN_LOCK_TIMEOUT_S=600 at :232), so every later message — voice, text, MCP — gets 'The previous turn is still running' forever; only restarting the process recovers.
